('Level8_2','Level8_2_4408','forecast','''fɔrkæst','''fɔːkɑːst','[v] 预报，预测；预示; [n] 预测，预报；预想','Rain was forecast for the weekend.  预报周末有雨。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_4409','forecourt','','''fɔːkɔːt','[n] 前院；前场','The graveled forecourt in front of the manor was crowded with cars, and they weren''t nun cars.  庄园前院挤满了高档轿车，而且它们肯定不可能时修女们能负担地的起的。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_4410','forefinger','''fɔrfɪŋɡɚ','''fɔːfɪŋgə','[n] 食指','He took the pen between his thumb and forefinger.  他用拇指和食指夹起笔。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_4411','forefront','''fɔrfrʌnt','''fɔːfrʌnt','[n] 最前线，最前部；活动的中心','They have been at the forefront of the campaign for political change.  他们一直处于政治变革运动的前沿。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_4412','forego','fɔ:,ɡəu','fɔ:,ɡəu','[v] 放弃；居先；在……之前','Many skiers are happy to forego a summer holiday to go skiing.  许多滑雪者乐于放弃暑假去滑雪。'),
