('Level8_2','Level8_2_5635','imagery','''ɪmɪdʒəri','''ɪmɪdʒ(ə)rɪ','[n] 像；意象；比喻；形象化','Their dreams commonly involved complex stories with visual imagery.  他们的梦里常常有很多复杂的情节，充满了生动的画面。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5636','imaginable','ɪ''mædʒɪnəbl','ɪ''mædʒɪnəb(ə)l','[adj] 可能的；可想像的','The travel brochure is full of the most wonderful resorts imaginable.  这本旅游小册子里全是人们梦寐以求的最好的旅游胜地。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5637','imaginary','ɪ''mædʒɪnɛri','ɪ''mædʒɪn(ə)rɪ','[adj] 虚构的，假想的；想像的；虚数的','As she listened, she played an imaginary piano on her knees.  她边听边在膝盖上作弹钢琴状。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5638','imagination','ɪ,mædʒɪ''neʃən','ɪ,mædʒɪ''neɪʃ(ə)n','[n] [心理] 想象力；空想；幻想物','a storyteller with an incredible imagination  想象力极丰富的讲故事者'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5639','imaginative','ɪ''mædʒɪnətɪv','ɪ''mædʒɪnətɪv','[adj] 富于想象的；有创造力的','an imaginative use of computer technology  计算机技术的妙用'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5640','imagine','ɪ''mædʒɪn','ɪ''mædʒɪn','[v] 想像；猜想；臆断','Perhaps she’d never really been there at all – perhaps she’d just imagined it.  可能她从未到过那儿——也许这都是她的幻想。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5641','imbalance','ɪm''bæləns','ɪm''bæl(ə)ns','[n] 不平衡；不安定','a hormonal imbalance  内分泌失调'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5642','imbecile','''ɪmbɪsaɪl','''ɪmbɪsiːl','[n] 低能者；愚蠢的人; [adj] 低能的；愚笨的；虚弱的','He looked at me as if I was a total imbecile.  他看着我，好像我是个大笨蛋。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5643','imbecility',',ɪmbə''sɪləti',',ɪmbɪ''sɪlətɪ','[n] 愚钝；低能；愚蠢的行为，言语等',''),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5644','imbibe','ɪm''baɪb','ɪm''baɪb','[v] 吸收，接受；喝；吸入','Both men imbibed considerable quantities of gin.  这两个男人都喝了大量的杜松子酒。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5645','imbue','ɪm''bjʊ','ɪm''bjuː','[v] 灌输；使感染；使渗透','The film is imbued with the star''s rebellious spirit.  这部电影充满了那位明星的反叛精神。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5646','imitate','''ɪmɪtet','''ɪmɪteɪt','[v] 模仿，仿效；仿造，仿制','She was a splendid mimic and loved to imitate Winston Churchill.  她是个出色的模仿者，喜欢模仿温斯顿·丘吉尔。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5647','imitation',',ɪmɪ''teʃən','ɪmɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 模仿，仿造；仿制品; [adj] 人造的，仿制的','The remake of ‘Casablanca’ was a pale imitation (= something that is much less good than the thing it imitates ) of the original movie.  重拍的《卡萨布兰卡》远不如原版。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5648','immaculate','ɪ''mækjələt','ɪ''mækjʊlət','[adj] 完美的；洁净的；无瑕疵的','her immaculate stage performances  她完美的舞台表演'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5649','immaterial',',ɪmə''tɪrɪəl','ɪmə''tɪərɪəl','[adj] 非物质的；无形的；不重要的；非实质的','If you sign a document, it is wholly immaterial whether you have read it carefully or not.  文件一经签署，是否仔细阅读过文件就完全无关紧要了。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5650','immature',',ɪmə''tʃʊr',',ɪmə''tjʊə; ,ɪmə''tjɔː','[adj] 不成熟的；未成熟的；粗糙的','He forgave his son’s immature behaviour.  他原谅了儿子的幼稚行为。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5651','immeasurable','ɪ''mɛʒərəbl','ɪ''meʒ(ə)rəb(ə)l','[adj] 无限的；[数] 不可计量的；不能测量的','The refugee problem has now reached immeasurable proportions.  难民问题现在已经到了无法估量的程度。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5652','immediate','ɪ''midɪət','ɪ''miːdɪət','[adj] 立即的；直接的；最接近的','Our immediate response to the attack was sheer horror.  我们对攻击的第一反应就是非常惊恐。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5653','immediately','ɪ''midɪətli','ɪ''miːdɪətlɪ','[adv] 立即，立刻；直接地; [conj] 一…就','Mix in the remaining ingredients and serve immediately.  拌入余下的食材，立即上桌。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5654','immense','ɪ''mɛns','ɪ''mens','[adj] 巨大的，广大的；无边无际的；非常好的','People who travel by rail still read an immense amount.  人们坐火车旅行时仍然会读很多书。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5655','immerse','ɪ''mɝs','ɪ''mɜːs','[v] 沉浸；使陷入','The electrodes are immersed in liquid.  电极被浸没在液体中。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5656','immigrant','''ɪmɪɡrənt','''ɪmɪgr(ə)nt','[adj] 移民的；迁入的; [n] 移民，侨民','But “the hostile part can be mobilized from time to time,” by what he calls “anti-immigrant entrepreneurs.  但是“敌对的那部分可能会不时地动员”，以他称之为“反移民企业家”的名义。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5657','immigrate','''ɪmɪɡret','''ɪmɪgreɪt','[v] 移入','His father and mother immigrated when he was two.  他的父母在他两岁时移民到这里。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5658','immigration',',ɪmɪ''ɡreʃən','ɪmɪ''ɡreɪʃn','[n] 外来移民；移居','He called for a common European policy on immigration.  他要求欧洲国家实施共同的移民政策。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5659','imminent','''ɪmɪnənt','''ɪmɪnənt','[adj] 即将来临的；迫近的','A new trade agreement is imminent.  一项新的贸易协定即将签署。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5660','immobile','ɪ''mobl','ɪ''məʊbaɪl','[adj] 固定的；稳定的；不变的','She could see a figure sitting immobile, facing the sea.  她看到一个人影面朝大海坐着，一动不动。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5661','immoral','ɪ''mɔrəl','ɪ''mɒr(ə)l','[adj] 不道德的；邪恶的；淫荡的','Deliberately making people suffer is immoral.  故意使人吃苦头是不道德的。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5662','immortal','ɪ''mɔrtl','ɪ''mɔːt(ə)l','[adj] 不朽的；神仙的；长生的; [n] 神仙；不朽人物','Plato believed that the soul is immortal.  柏拉图认为灵魂不灭。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5663','immune','ɪ''mjʊn','ɪ''mjuːn','[adj] 免疫的；免于……的，免除的; [n] 免疫者；免除者','Once we’ve had the disease, we’re immune for life.  我们一旦得过这种病，就获得了终身免疫力。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5664','immunize','''ɪmjʊ''naɪz','''imju:naiz','[v] 使免疫；赋予免疫性','We should require that every student is immunized against hepatitis B.  我们应该要求每一位学生都注射乙肝疫苗。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5665','impact','ɪm''pækt','''ɪmpækt','[n] 影响；效果；碰撞；冲击力; [v] 挤入，压紧；撞击；对…产生影响','The force of the impact knocked the breath out of her.  撞击力使她喘不过气来。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5666','impair','ɪm''pɛr','ɪm''peə','[v] 损害；削弱；减少','The illness had impaired his ability to think and concentrate.  这种疾病损害了他的思维能力和注意力。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5667','impale','im''peil','ɪm''peɪl','[v] 刺穿；钉住；使绝望','Researchers observed one bird impale a rodent on a cactus.  研究人员观察到，一只鸟把一个啮齿动物钉到了一棵仙人掌上。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5668','impart','ɪm''pɑrt','ɪm''pɑːt','[v] 给予（尤指抽象事物），传授；告知，透露','She had information that she couldn’t wait to impart.  她得到了消息，迫不及待地想告诉别人。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5669','impartial','ɪm''pɑrʃəl','ɪm''pɑːʃ(ə)l','[adj] 公平的，公正的；不偏不倚的','We offer impartial advice on tax and insurance.  我们就税收和保险问题提供公充的建议。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5670','impasse','''ɪmpæs','æm''pɑːs; ''æmpɑːs','[n] 僵局；死路','Negotiations seemed to have reached an impasse.  谈判似乎陷入了僵局。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5671','impassioned','ɪm''pæʃnd','ɪm''pæʃ(ə)nd','[adj] 充满激情的；感激的; [v] 使充满激情（impassion的过去式和过去分词）','She appeared on television to make an impassioned plea for help.  她在电视上恳切地请求人们帮助。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5672','impassive','ɪm''pæsɪv','ɪm''pæsɪv','[adj] 冷漠的；无感觉的','Her impassive face showed no reaction at all.  她表情冷淡，毫无反应。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5673','impatience','ɪm''peʃəns','ɪm''peɪʃns','[n] 急躁；无耐心','A note of impatience had entered his voice.  他的语气开始透出一丝不耐烦。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5674','impeach','ɪm''pitʃ','ɪm''piːtʃ','[v] 弹劾；归咎；怀疑; [n] 控告，检举；弹劾；怀疑','The governor was impeached for using state funds improperly.  州长因违规使用州政府资金而受到弹劾。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5675','impeccable','ɪm''pɛkəbl','ɪm''pekəb(ə)l','[adj] 无瑕疵的；没有缺点的','She has taught her children impeccable manners.  她把她的孩子教育得举止十分得体。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5676','impede','ɪm''pid','ɪm''piːd','[v] 阻碍；妨碍；阻止','Storms at sea impeded our progress.  海上风暴阻碍了我们的航程。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5677','impediment','ɪm''pɛdɪmənt','ɪm''pedɪm(ə)nt','[n] 口吃；妨碍；阻止','He was satisfied that there was no legal impediment to the marriage.  他对于这场婚姻没有法律上的障碍感到很满意。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5678','impel','ɪm''pɛl','ɪm''pel','[v] 推动；驱使；激励','...the courage and competitiveness which impels him to take risks.  ...驱策他冒险的勇气和竞争精神。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5679','impending','ɪm''pɛndɪŋ','ɪm''pendɪŋ','[adj] 即将发生的；迫切的；悬挂的; [v] 迫近；悬空（impend的现在分词）','On the morning of the expedition, I awoke with a feeling of impending disaster.  远征出发的那天早上，我醒来就有一种大难临头的感觉。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5680','impenetrable','ɪm''pɛnɪtrəbl','ɪm''penɪtrəb(ə)l','[adj] 不能通过的；顽固的；费解的；不接纳的','The trees formed a dark and impenetrable barrier.  这些树形成了一道无法通过的黑暗屏障。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5681','imperative','ɪm''pɛrətɪv','ɪm''perətɪv','[adj] 必要的，不可避免的；紧急的；命令的，专横的；势在必行的；[语]祈使的; [n] 必要的事；命令；需要；规则；[语]祈使语气','It is imperative that politicians should be good communicators.  政治家应该是很好的沟通者，这很重要。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5682','imperceptible',',ɪmpɚ''sɛptəbl','ɪmpə''septɪb(ə)l','[adj] 感觉不到的；极细微的','Such changes are imperceptible to even the best-trained eye.  这样的变化即使是对最训练有素的人来说也不易察觉。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5683','imperfect','ɪm''pɝfɪkt','ɪm''pɜːfɪkt','[adj] 有缺点的；未完成的；半过去的；未完成时的; [n] 未完成体; [adv] 有瑕疵地；有缺点地','the imperfect world we live in  我们生活于其中的不完美的世界'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5684','imperial','ɪm''pɪrɪəl','ɪm''pɪərɪəl','[adj] 帝国的；皇帝的；至高无上的；威严的; [n] 纸张尺寸；特等品','Britain’s imperial expansion in the 19th century  19世纪英帝国的扩张'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5685','imperialism','ɪm''pɪrɪəlɪzəm','ɪm''pɪərɪəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 帝国主义','a book on the history of British imperialism  一本关于英国帝国主义历史的书'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5686','imperialist','ɪm''pɪrɪəlɪst','ɪm''pɪərɪəlɪst','[n] 帝国主义者; [adj] 帝国主义的','He claims that imperialists are trying to re-establish colonial rule in the country.  他声称帝国主义者正试图在该国重建殖民统治。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5687','imperil','ɪm''pɛrəl','ɪm''perɪl; -r(ə)l','[v] 危及；使陷于危险','Tax increases now might imperil economic recovery.  目前提高税收可能会危及经济的复苏。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5688','imperious','ɪm''pɪrɪəs','ɪm''pɪərɪəs','[adj] 专横的；迫切的；傲慢的','She raised her hand in an imperious gesture.  她傲慢地扬起手。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5689','impersonal','ɪm''pɝsnl','ɪm''pɜːs(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 客观的；非个人的；没有人情味的；非人称的; [n] 非人称动词；不具人格的事物','Business letters do not have to be impersonal and formal.  商业信函并非一定要刻板而缺乏人情味。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5690','impersonate','ɪm''pɝsənet','ɪm''pɜːs(ə)neɪt','[v] 扮演；模仿；拟人，人格化','In the film he amusingly impersonates a woman.  影片中他模仿一个女人，非常好笑。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5691','impertinent','ɪm''pɝtnənt','ɪm''pɜːtɪnənt','[adj] 不恰当的；无礼的；粗鲁的；不相干的','He was always asking impertinent questions.  他老是问一些唐突的问题。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5692','impetuous','ɪm''pɛtʃʊəs','ɪm''petjʊəs','[adj] 冲动的；鲁莽的；猛烈的','He was high-spirited and impetuous.  他情绪高昂，行事鲁莽。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5693','impetus','''ɪmpɪtəs','''ɪmpɪtəs','[n] 动力；促进；冲力','The discovery gave fresh impetus to the research.  这个发现为研究带来新动力。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5694','impinge','ɪm''pɪndʒ','ɪm''pɪn(d)ʒ','[v] 撞击；侵犯','Yet if those systems seriously impinge on people’s freedom, many people will balk.  然而如果这些系统严重侵犯了人们的自由的话，许多人将会停滞不前。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5695','impious','''ɪmpɪəs','''ɪmpɪəs; ɪm''paɪəs','[adj] 不虔诚的；不孝的；不敬的','an impious crime  大不敬之罪'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5696','implacable','ɪm''plækəbl','ɪm''plækəb(ə)l','[adj] 不能安抚的；难和解的；不能缓和的','implacable enemies  死敌'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5697','implant','ɪm''plænt','ɪm''plɑːnt','[v] 种植；灌输；嵌入; [n] [医] 植入物；植入管','Surgeons successfully implanted an artificial hip.  外科医生成功地植入了一个人工髋关节。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5698','implement','''ɪmplɪmɛnt','''ɪmplɪm(ə)nt','[v] 实施，执行；实现，使生效; [n] 工具，器具；手段','The government promised to implement a new system to control financial loan institutions.  政府许诺要实施新的制度来控制金融贷款机构。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5699','implicate','''ɪmplɪket','''ɪmplɪkeɪt','[v] 使卷入；涉及；暗指；影响',''),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5700','implication','''ɪmplɪ''keʃən','ɪmplɪ''keɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 含义；暗示；牵连，卷入；可能的结果，影响','This election has profound implications for the future of U.S. democracy.  对于美国民主的未来而言，这次选举影响深远。'),
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO words (book_slug, slug, word, phonetic_us, phonetic_uk, meaning, example) VALUES,
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5701','implicit','ɪm''plɪsɪt','ɪm''plɪsɪt','[adj] 含蓄的；暗示的；盲从的','...an implicit warning to the Moroccans not to continue or repeat the military actions they began a week ago.  …叫摩洛哥人不要继续或重复一周前开始的军事行动的含蓄警告。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5702','implore','ɪm''plɔr','ɪm''plɔː','[v] 恳求或乞求','‘Don’t go,’ I implored her.  “不要走。”我哀求她。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5703','imply','ɪm''plai','ɪm''plaɪ','[v] 意味；暗示；隐含','an implied threat  隐含的威胁'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5704','impolite','ˌɪmpəˈlaɪt','ɪmpə''laɪt','[adj] 无礼的；粗鲁的','an impolite remark  无礼的话'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5705','import','''ɪmpɔt','ɪm''pɔːt; ''ɪm-','[n] 进口，进口货；输入；意思，含义；重要性; [v] 输入，进口；含…的意思',''),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5706','importance','ɪm''pɔrtns','ɪm''pɔːt(ə)ns','[n] 价值；重要；重大；傲慢','He was full of his own importance (= he behaved in an annoying way which showed that he thought he was very important ).  他自以为很了不起。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5707','important','ɪm''pɔrtnt','ɪm''pɔːt(ə)nt','[adj] 重要的，重大的；有地位的；有权力的','a very important meeting  很重要的会议'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5708','importer','ɪm''pɔrtɚ','','[n] 进口商；输入者','Japan is the biggest importer of U.S. beef.  日本是美国牛肉的最大进口国。'),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5709','impose','ɪm''poz','ɪm''pəʊz','[v] 利用；欺骗；施加影响',''),
('Level8_2','Level8_2_5710','imposing','ɪm''pozɪŋ','ɪm''pəʊzɪŋ','[adj] （建筑物等）壮观的；威风的；（仪表）堂堂的；给人深刻印象的; [v] impose的ing形式','He was an imposing man.  他是个仪表堂堂的男子汉。'),
