('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_125','propose','prə''poz','prə''pəuz','[v] 提议， 建议； 提名， 推荐； 打算； 求婚','the changes currently proposed by the local planning authorities  目前由地方规划局提议的改革'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_126','in comparison with','','','与…比较，同…比较起来','Alexander and Gaius and Pompeius, what are they in comparison with Diogenes and Heraclitus and Socrates?  亚历山大、盖耶斯和庞培与第欧根尼、赫拉克利特、苏格拉底比较起来是什么人呢？'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_127','fallow','''fælo','''fæləu','[adj] 休耕的； 休闲的','They let the land lie fallow for a year.  他们让土地休耕一年。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_128','renewable','rɪ''nuəbl','rɪ''njuːəbl','[adj] 可更新的， 可再生的， 可恢复的； 可延长有效期的， 可续期的','It’s a six-month lease but it’s renewable.  租期六个月，但是可以续签。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_129','malevolent','mə''lɛvələnt','mə''levələnt','[adj] 有恶意的； 恶毒的','Her stare was malevolent, her mouth a thin line.  她目光狠毒，嘴唇紧闭。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_130','ensue','ɪn''su','ɪn''sjuː','[vi] 继而发生； 接着发生','If the Europeans did not reduce subsidies, a trade war would ensue.  如果欧洲不减少补贴，贸易战将随即爆发。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_131','foreseeable','fɔr''siəbl','fɔː''siːəbl','[adj] 可预知的， 能预测的','The judge found that it was not foreseeable that the fuel would catch fire.  法官裁定，燃料着火是无法预料的。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_132','coach','kotʃ','kəutʃ','[n] 教练；指导；长途汽车; [vt] 训练； 辅导','a tennis coach  网球教练'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_133','pine','paɪn','paɪn','[v] 难过，','Six months after he left, she was still pining.  他离开六个月了，她还是很悲伤。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_134','carousel','''kærə''sɛl','ˌkærə''sel','[n] 行李式传送带',''),
