('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_591','semantic','sɪ''mæntɪk','sɪ''mæntɪk','[adj] 语义的','He did not want to enter into a semantic debate.  他不想卷入一场关于语义的争论。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_592','upset','ʌp''sɛt','ʌp''s3t','[adj] 心烦的； 不适的; [vt] 使苦恼；搅乱；推翻，颠倒[ˌʌp''s3t]','You’re not still upset with me, are you?  你不是还在生我的气吧？'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_593','dot','dɑt','dɒt','[v] 打点于； 散布于， 点缀; [n] 点，小圆点','Poppies dotted the field.  田野里遍布着星星点点的罂粟花。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_594','skim','skɪm','skɪm','[v] 撇去； 掠过， 擦过； 浏览， 略读','Julie skimmed the sports page.  朱莉浏览了体育版。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_595','stamp','stæmp','stæmp','[v] 跺，重踏；在…上盖；','The audience stamped and shouted.  观众又是跺脚又是高声叫喊。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_596','skip','skɪp','skɪp','[v] 跳， 蹦； 漏过； 逃学','I decided to skip the first chapter.  我决定跳过第一章。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_597','disseminate','dɪ''sɛmɪnet','dɪ''semɪneɪt','[v] 散布， 传播','Her findings have been widely disseminated .  她的发现已广为传播。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_598','exodus','''ɛksədəs','''eksədəs','[n] 大批离去， 成群外出','The medical system is facing collapse because of an exodus of doctors.  由于医生大批离去，该医疗体系正面临崩溃。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_599','mention','''mɛnʃən','''menʃn','[n&v] 提及， 说起','Was my name mentioned at all?  我的名字被提到过吗？'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_600','stream','strim','striːm','[v] 流出; [n] 溪流；一股','Tears streamed down their faces.  泪水顺着他们的脸颊流下来。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_601','laundry','''lɔndri','''lɔːndri','[n] 洗衣房； 待洗衣服','She did the laundry (= washed the clothes etc ) and hung it out to dry.  她洗了衣服，然后挂出去晾干。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_602','grudge','ɡrʌdʒ','grʌdʒ','[n] 不满，积怨，','He appears to have a grudge against certain players.  他好像对某些选手有积怨。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_603','accumulate','ə''kjumjəlet','ə''kjuːmjəleɪt','[v] 积累； 堆积','It is unjust that a privileged few should continue to accumulate wealth.  少数特权阶级继续积聚财富，这是不公平的。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_604','crime','kraɪm','kraɪm','[n] 罪行； 犯罪','We moved here because there was very little crime.  我们搬到这里来是因为这里的犯罪率很低。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_605','surround','sə''raʊnd','sə''raund','[vt] 围绕； 包围','He glared at the people who surrounded the tent.  他怒视着围住帐篷的那些人。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_606','leisure','''liʒɚ','''leʒə(r)','[n] 空闲时间； 悠闲','Most people now enjoy shorter working hours and more leisure time.  现在大多数人都喜欢工作时间短些，闲暇时间多些。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_607','pavement','''pevmənt','''peɪvmənt','[n] 人行道； 地面， 路面','A small group of journalists waited on the pavement outside her house.  有一小群记者守候在她家外面的人行道上。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_608','undetected','''ʌndɪ''tɛktɪd','ˌʌndɪ''tektɪd','[adj] 未被发现的','The thieves escaped undetected through a basement window.  那些盗贼从地下室的窗户神不知鬼不觉地逃走了。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_609','irregularity','ɪ''rɛgjə''lærəti','ɪˌregjə''lærəti','[n] 不规则， 无规律','Its complexity degree can be quantitatively evaluated using fractal dimension that can describe geometrical irregularity.  其复杂程度可以用描述几何不规则性的分维来定量评价。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_610','assimilate','ə''sɪməlet','ə''sɪməleɪt','[v] 吸收； 使同化','It will take time to assimilate all these facts.  充分掌握所有这些情况需要时间。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_611','ethical','''ɛθɪkl','''eθɪkl','[adj] 道德的； 伦理的','The president must have the highest ethical standards.  总统必须具备最高的道德水准。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_612','cultivation','''kʌltə''veʃən','ˌkʌltɪ''veɪʃn','[n] 耕种， 耕作； 培养， 教育','soil cultivation  土壤耕作'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_613','addict','''ædɪkt (for n.); əˈdɪkt (for v.)','''ædɪkt','[n] 吸毒成瘾的人， 有瘾的人， 对…入迷的人','He''s only 24 years old and a drug addict.  他只有24岁，可已经是一个瘾君子。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_614','marvellous','''mɑrvələs','''mɑːvələs','[n] 令人惊奇的； 奇特的， 非凡的； 奇迹般的， 不可思议的； 绝妙的',''),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_615','aluminium',',æljə''mɪnɪəm','ˌæljə''mɪniəm','[n] 铝','recycled aluminium cans  再生铝罐'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_616','trustworthy','''trʌstwɝði','''trʌstwɜːði','[adj] 值得信赖的， 可靠的','He is a trustworthy and level-headed leader.  他是个可信赖的、头脑冷静的领导。'),
('IELTS_3','IELTS_3_617','comparable','''kɑmpərəbl','''kɒmpərəbl','[adj] 可比较的， 类似的； 比得上的','A car of comparable size would cost far more abroad.  同样大小的汽车在国外要贵得多。'),
